 "notes": "Black-hole superradiance limit on the axion, Fig. 1 (mainlim.jpeg in e-print), plotted directly in (m_a [eV], 1/f_a [GeV^-1]). Reported curve is the upper envelope of the dark-blue FIDUCIAL excluded region (n<=5, 2sigma), which the caption states covers only the m<=2 spin-down region and is the paper's robust headline result; the lighter/grey shaded lobe extending to ~1.1e-11 eV (m>2, higher-order levels) is flagged by the authors as less certain and is NOT included here. Limit derived from Cyg X-1 (conservative spin) + GRS 1915+105; the two dark-blue lobes with a pinch/notch near ~3.4e-12 eV correspond to the two black holes. Region is excluded for all 1/f_a below this envelope (fill extends to bottom of frame), so only the upper boundary is digitized. White dashed curve = previous constraints of Ref.[44], not traced. Axes calibrated from major ticks; raster JPEG read by pixel color mask on RGB[0,33,71]. Superradiance is gravitational, so no DM-density dependence (dm_density_assumed null).",
